usage: cli.py [-h] [--state STATE] [--json] [--remote-profile REMOTE_PROFILE]
              [--local]
              {init,doctor,submit,list,status,logs,cancel,report,rerun,retry,compare,recover,stop,scan,auth,catalog,usage,attachments,artifacts,download,service}
              ...

Harbor experiments on a shared Linux/Docker machine

positional arguments:
  {init,doctor,submit,list,status,logs,cancel,report,rerun,retry,compare,recover,stop,scan,auth,catalog,usage,attachments,artifacts,download,service}
    init                Initialize team configuration once
    doctor              Check dependencies/sources without calling a model
    submit              Freeze inputs and submit detached Harbor work
    recover             Restart/reconcile scheduler after a crash
    stop                Stop idle scheduler so maintainer can refresh runtime
                        credentials
    scan                Scan stopped team state; safe counts only
    auth                Account-local team login (no provider probe)
    catalog             Shared service metadata
    usage               Shared service metadata
    attachments         Shared service attachment versions
    artifacts           Shared service artifacts
    download            Download safe service artifact (new file only)
    service             Shared HTTP service / remote member login

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --state STATE         Team state directory
  --json                Original machine-readable output
  --remote-profile REMOTE_PROFILE
                        Use named service member profile
  --local               Explicitly use original local CLI
